    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "11c2b9ee57214205995a78388e5a5032",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Two averaging conventions</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The reference divides each incoming polarization sum by two:\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\overline{|\\mathcal M|^2}_{2} =\n\\frac{(D-2)^2 N_c^2 g_s^4(t^2+tu+u^2)^3}\n{(N_c^2-1)s^2t^2u^2},\\qquad s+t+u=0.||)</marimo-tex>$\nAveraging over all <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D-2||)</marimo-tex> physical incoming states instead multiplies this\nresult by <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(4/(D-2)^2||)</marimo-tex>. These conventions agree at <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(N_c=3||)</marimo-tex>, the result equals\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\frac92 g_s^4(3-tu/s^2-su/t^2-st/u^2)||)</marimo-tex>.\nThe exact comparison also checks exchange of the identical outgoing gluons.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
