          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Four-dimensional angular-cut event rates</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The rate uses <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4||)</marimo-tex> with native flux and two-body phase space, the full\nazimuth integral and the <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/2!||)</marimo-tex> factor for identical final gluons:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\\frac{d\\sigma}{d\\cos\\theta}=\\frac{\\overline{|\\mathcal M|^2}}{64\\pi s}.||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">This lower panel always uses four dimensions, independently of the amplitude\ndisplay above. We show <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s\\sigma/\\alpha_s^2||)</marimo-tex>, with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(g_s^2=4\\pi\\alpha_s||)</marimo-tex>.\nThe cut <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(|\\cos\\theta|&lt;c&lt;1||)</marimo-tex> excludes the massless exchange poles.\nSymbolica integrates the angular density; nine independent Gaussian\nquadratures verify the color and cut choices below.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
